 "note": "Splits constructed to TILE THE DIFFICULTY RANGE on both sides. Split unit = complex (never divided, to avoid antibody/antigen leakage). Bands = tertiles of complex median rescue rank. 8q3j (the most extreme complex) was assigned to TRAIN so the method is developed with knowledge of the hardest regime; 8vzo swapped to TEST to preserve the 5/5/5 complex balance. Test is never used for tuning. | 2026-07-12 CORRECTION: 8a67_AD DROPPED for ONE reason only \u2014 no consistent pose-pose matrix can exist for it. OST maps its native chain A onto model chains of BOTH 72 and 76 residues (different molecules, not copies), so different poses would contribute different proteins to the same matrix. Rarity of acceptable poses is NOT an exclusion criterion: 8vvl_AC, 7z1x_AB, 7uvs_BC and 8be1_AC each have exactly 1 acceptable pose and are KEPT \u2014 they are the hardest and most informative cases. 48 -> 47 interfaces. Difficulty recomputed on the corrected matrices, where a pose must HAVE interface contacts to count as acceptable."
